# Content UI

The shell (topbar, sidebar, drawer) and the inner pages follow the Graphite identity (`DESIGN.md`; spec `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-09-graphite-identity.md`). Inner canvas pages compose the shared components below and lay them out with Tailwind utilities; they do not write their own card, table, tab or dialog look (ADR 0022).

- Page title: `Desk` (`components/desk.tsx`) with one `title` and an optional `lede`. Do not repeat the header greeting.
- Section: `Pane` (`components/desk.tsx`). One card style.
- Tabs: `Tabs` (`components/tabs.tsx` on `components/ui/tabs.tsx`). A segmented pick is `Segmented` (`components/ui/segmented.tsx`).
- Workbench: a `FilterBar` (`components/filter-bar.tsx`) that is a direct child of the desk, followed by a `Pane`, is one surface. The bar is the head; the pane is the body. Do not give the bar its own card shadow.
- Filters: `FilterBar`, above the table, never inside the table head. Filters apply as the user changes them.
- Scroll: the shell is `100dvh` with `overflow: hidden`. Workbench lists (the desk → `FilterBar` + `Pane` + `TableSheet`) fill the canvas and **the table sheet scrolls**. Multi-block pages (the desk → a stack of panes) size to content and **the canvas scrolls**. Do not give the last stack pane `flex-1` / crush it — that creates a dead scrollport.
- Table: `DataTable` / `PagedTable` (`components/data-table.tsx` on `components/ui/table.tsx`). Text and status align to the start. Numeric columns set `num` (tabular figures on the header and the cell), values use `Money` when they are money. Phone numbers, logins, and other Latin identifiers stay in `<bdi dir="ltr">`. The operations column sets `actions` and holds the `RowMenu`. Do not clip names or amounts.
- Row actions: `RowMenu` from `components/row-menu.tsx` is the only per-row trigger. Pass a label that names the record. Destructive items use `danger` and an icon. Page-level actions, such as creating a record, stay visible. An inline price field (`PriceField`) keeps its own save control.
- Status: `<Badge variant={tone} dot>` (`components/ui/badge.tsx`) with a text label; the tone comes from `lib/status-tone.ts`.
- Dialog: `Dialog` from `components/dialog.tsx`. Sizes are `confirm`, `form` (default, about 560px), and `wide`. Put fields in the children and actions in `footer` (`secondary` cancel, then `primary` save: the cluster at the inline end, the action at the far end; `DESIGN.md`, ADR 0021 D8). A dialog with several independent operations keeps destructive actions in the footer. Checkboxes and radios are `Checkbox` / `RadioGroup` (`components/ui/`); do not give them text-field dimensions. Do not build a second overlay: side panels are `Sheet`, popups `Popover` / `DropdownMenu` / `Tooltip` (`components/ui/`).
- Fields: `Field`, `Label`, `Input`, `Textarea`, `Select`, `DateField`, `PriceField`, `NameField`. A dropdown is always `Select`, never a bare `<select>`.
- Empty: `EmptyState` (`components/empty-state.tsx`) inside the pane; a failed load is `LoadFailed`. It carries its own padding; never add padding around it.

Tokens stay `--rd-*` in `apps/web/app/tailwind.css`, the only stylesheet, and are used through their Tailwind names (`bg-surface`, `text-muted`). Arabic and Latin text stays Noto Kufi Arabic, Hebrew stays IBM Plex Sans Hebrew, and numbers use tabular figures (`tabular-nums`) on the same font. No new font and no raw hex.
